window.docContents[187].resolve({"/Exponential___-Logarithmic___-Sine___-and-Cosine-Integrals/___6___16-Mathematical-Applications/#LMLF-___-DLMF-with-Lean--Exponential___-Logarithmic___-Sine___-and-Cosine-Integrals--___6___16-Mathematical-Applications--___6___16-Mathematical-Applications":{"contents":"This section applies sine-integral and logarithmic-integral methods to two\nclassical topics: the Gibbs phenomenon and the relation between the\nlogarithmic integral and prime counting. All limits and order estimates retain\nthe real domains and hypotheses stated by the DLMF.\n\n\n\n\n\n","context":"LMLF · DLMF with Lean\u0009Exponential, Logarithmic, Sine, and Cosine Integrals\u0009§6.16 Mathematical Applications","header":"§6.16 Mathematical Applications","id":"/Exponential___-Logarithmic___-Sine___-and-Cosine-Integrals/___6___16-Mathematical-Applications/#LMLF-___-DLMF-with-Lean--Exponential___-Logarithmic___-Sine___-and-Cosine-Integrals--___6___16-Mathematical-Applications--___6___16-Mathematical-Applications"},"/Exponential___-Logarithmic___-Sine___-and-Cosine-Integrals/___6___9-Continued-Fraction/#LMLF-___-DLMF-with-Lean--Exponential___-Logarithmic___-Sine___-and-Cosine-Integrals--___6___9-Continued-Fraction--___6___9-Continued-Fraction":{"contents":"DLMF §6.9 records the principal exponential integral E_1(z) as a\ncontinued fraction in the open principal cut plane\n|\\operatorname{ph}z|<\\pi, with z ≠ 0 as required by the defining\nexponential-integral value. The display uses the standard alternating\npartial denominators (z,1,z,1,\\ldots) and repeated numerators\n(1,1,2,2,3,3,\\ldots). Its convergence is represented below through the\nshared finite continued-fraction evaluator, with the principal E_1 value specified by the\ncanonical §6.2 map principalE1.\n\nThe continued fraction has the exact DLMF form\nE_1(z)=\\frac{e^{-z}}{z+\\cfrac{1}{1+\\cfrac{1}{z+\\cfrac{2}{1+\\cfrac{2}{z+\\cfrac{3}{1+\\cfrac{3}{z+\\cdots}}}}}}},\\qquad |\\operatorname{ph}z|<\\pi.$$\nHere \\operatorname{ph}z is the principal phase; its strict bound excludes the\nnegative-real cut, while the explicit nonzero hypothesis excludes the origin.\nThe Lean disclosure uses the shared\ncontinuedFractionConvergent evaluator with denominator stream z,1,z,1,...\nand numerator stream 1,1,2,2,3,3,...; its optional offset remains available\nfor genuine tails. The theorem states that the resulting convergents tend to\nthe canonical principal E_1 map.\n\nThe source cites Nielsen (1906b, pp. 42–44) and Lorentzen and Waadeland\n(1992, p. 577) for the continued fraction.\n\nSection 6.9 presents the continued fraction for the principal exponential\nintegral in the strict principal-phase domain |ph z| < π.\n\nThe source also points to Cuyt et al. (2008, pp. 287–290) for this continued\nfraction.\n\n","context":"LMLF · DLMF with Lean\u0009Exponential, Logarithmic, Sine, and Cosine Integrals\u0009§6.9 Continued Fraction","header":"§6.9 Continued Fraction","id":"/Exponential___-Logarithmic___-Sine___-and-Cosine-Integrals/___6___9-Continued-Fraction/#LMLF-___-DLMF-with-Lean--Exponential___-Logarithmic___-Sine___-and-Cosine-Integrals--___6___9-Continued-Fraction--___6___9-Continued-Fraction"}});